{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoQ62RUHL5bgtKFkHcAKpG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# PRD: Commentary Talent CRM\n     2→\n     3→**Status:** NOT STARTED\n     4→**Date:** 2026-03-10\n     5→**Last Updated:** 2026-03-10\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Overview\n    10→A full-stack CRM for coordinating 15–20+ gymnastics commentary talent across a season: migrating the\n    11→existing 428-contact Google Sheet into Firebase, adding self-service booking links, Gmail/GCal outreach,\n    12→AI-powered talent discovery from alumni rosters, and automated pre-production alerts. Phase 1\n    13→(Talent Roster UI) is already complete.\n    14→\n    15→## Test Competition / URL\n    16→| Field | Value |\n    17→|-------|-------|\n    18→| Competition ID | (use most recent competition in Firebase) |\n    19→| Producer URL | `https://commentarygraphic.com/{compId}/producer` |\n    20→| Commentary URL | `https://commentarygraphic.com/{compId}/commentary` |\n    21→| Talent Roster | `https://commentarygraphic.com/talent` |\n    22→\n    23→---\n    24→\n    25→## Phase 0 — Data Migration\n    26→\n    27→### User Stories\n    28→- As a coordinator, I run a script once and all 428 people from my Google Sheet appear in the app — names, phones, emails, statuses, affiliations, and prior season counts.\n    29→- As a coordinator, the 28 people who filled out the 2026 survey already have their tech info (internet speed, mic type, Discord status) populated.\n    30→- As a coordinator, when I open a talent profile for someone like Tiara DeTommaso, I can see the meets she called last season in her history tab — that data came from the assignment sheet automatically.\n    31→- As a coordinator, when the script encounters messy data (a phone field that says \"Barb said no\", or a duplicate with two slightly different spellings), it flags it in a log rather than crashing.\n    32→\n    33→### Acceptance Criteria\n    34→- [ ] Running `node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js --dry-run` prints a summary (X created, Y enriched, Z assignments added, N flagged) without writing to Firebase\n    35→- [ ] Running without `--dry-run` writes all 428 contacts to `talentRoster/` in Firebase\n    36→- [ ] Survey responses (28 records) are merged into matching contacts by email\n    37→- [ ] Competition assignments appear in each talent's `competitionHistory` array\n    38→- [ ] Rows with malformed phone/email are flagged in a log file, not skipped silently\n    39→- [ ] Duplicate names (fuzzy match > 90%) are flagged rather than creating two records\n    40→\n    41→---\n    42→\n    43→## Phase 2 — Booking Links + Smart Availability\n    44→\n    45→### User Stories\n    46→- As a coordinator, I click \"Generate Booking Link\" next to an assignment on the Commentary page. The app creates a unique URL I can copy and send via text or email.\n    47→- As a talent invitee, I open the link on my phone (no login required) and see the event name, date, venue, and my assigned role. I click \"Yes, I'm available\" — that's it. The coordinator's app immediately shows me as Confirmed.\n    48→- As a talent invitee, I click \"No, not this one\" and the app shows me the next 5 upcoming competitions. I can check the ones I could do. That interest is saved and the coordinator sees it automatically.\n    49→- As a coordinator, I leave a note on a talent profile. The app parses that note and automatically flags her as interested in competitions mentioned in the note.\n    50→- As a coordinator, when I'm looking at who to assign to a meet, I can see an \"Interested\" badge next to people who already flagged that competition as available.\n    51→\n    52→### Acceptance Criteria\n    53→- [ ] \"Generate Booking Link\" button appears next to each assignment in the Commentary page\n    54→- [ ] Booking page at `/book/:token` loads without login and shows competition name, date, venue, and role\n    55→- [ ] Clicking \"Yes\" updates assignment status to `confirmed` in Firebase immediately\n    56→- [ ] Clicking \"No\" shows next 5 competitions with checkboxes; checking saves to `talentRoster/{id}/interested`\n    57→- [ ] Adding a note with a date mention (e.g., \"available late February\") extracts and saves date hints to `interestedDates`\n    58→- [ ] \"Interested\" badge appears in the talent search panel on CommentaryPage for people who flagged that competition\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→## Phase 3 — Gmail + Google Calendar\n    63→\n    64→### User Stories\n    65→- As a coordinator, I complete a one-time Gmail OAuth setup. After that, I can send invite emails directly from the CommentaryPage — they come from my own Gmail address.\n    66→- As a coordinator, every outreach button has a companion \"Copy for iMessage\" button that formats the message, copies it to clipboard, and logs it as sent when I confirm.\n    67→- As a coordinator, I upload a screenshot of a text thread. The app reads it and extracts availability mentions, updating that talent's profile automatically.\n    68→- As a coordinator, I click \"Send Briefing\" and the talent gets an email with: competition details, Virtius session URL, commentary talent view link, Discord room info, and pre-production meeting time.\n    69→- As a coordinator, I click \"Send Calendar Invite\" and the talent gets a GCal event for competition day, 1 hour before start, with Discord info in the description.\n    70→- As a coordinator, I pick a date for the pre-production call and click \"Schedule\" — a GCal invite goes to the talent's email and the meeting is logged in the app.\n    71→- As a coordinator, every email I send appears in the talent's communication log on their profile page.\n    72→\n    73→### Acceptance Criteria\n    74→- [ ] \"Send Invite\" button on CommentaryPage sends email from coordinator's Gmail account\n    75→- [ ] Every outreach button has a sibling \"Copy for iMessage\" button; confirming send logs the action\n    76→- [ ] Screenshot upload on TalentProfilePage extracts availability text via Claude API and surfaces it as a note with extracted dates\n    77→- [ ] \"Send Briefing\" sends a formatted email with all 5 required fields (competition, Virtius URL, commentary link, Discord, pre-prod time)\n    78→- [ ] \"Send Calendar Invite\" creates a GCal event 1 hour before competition start with Discord info\n    79→- [ ] \"Schedule Pre-Production\" creates a GCal event for the specified date/time\n    80→- [ ] All sent communications appear in a \"Communications\" tab on TalentProfilePage with timestamp and type\n    81→\n    82→### Environment Variables Required (Phase 3 prerequisite)\n    83→The coordinator server (`server/.env` on `44.193.31.120`) needs:\n    84→```\n    85→GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...\n    86→GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...\n    87→GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=...\n    88→```\n    89→\n    90→---\n    91→\n    92→## Phase 4 — AI-Powered Discovery\n    93→\n    94→### User Stories\n    95→- As a coordinator, I go to `/talent/discover`, select a school, and click \"Find Candidates.\" The app pulls the RTN alumni roster for that school.\n    96→- As a coordinator, I see a list of candidate cards with suitability scores (1–5) and a brief explanation: \"Strong candidate — competed for 4 years, has a gymnastics podcast, active on Instagram.\"\n    97→- As a coordinator, each card shows any social links Claude found (LinkedIn, Instagram) so I can quickly verify the person.\n    98→- As a coordinator, I click \"Add to Roster\" on a promising candidate. They're added with status `need-info` (or `has-contact` if Claude found an email).\n    99→- As a coordinator, if I run discovery on a school I've already run, the app recognizes existing records and shows \"already in roster\" on those cards.\n   100→\n   101→### Acceptance Criteria\n   102→- [ ] `/talent/discover` page loads with a school name picker\n   103→- [ ] Clicking \"Find Candidates\" fetches alumni data for the selected school and returns candidate cards\n   104→- [ ] Each card shows: name, score (1–5), explanation, social links (if found)\n   105→- [ ] \"Add to Roster\" creates a `talentRoster/` entry with status `need-info` or `has-contact`\n   106→- [ ] Re-running discovery for the same school shows \"already in roster\" badge on existing records (no duplicates)\n   107→\n   108→### Environment Variables Required (Phase 4 prerequisite)\n   109→```\n   110→ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...  (on coordinator server)\n   111→```\n   112→\n   113→---\n   114→\n   115→## Phase 5 — Annual Survey + Pre-Production Alerts\n   116→\n   117→### User Stories\n   118→- As a coordinator, at the start of each season I send talent a link to `/survey/2027`. They fill it out and their answers go directly into Firebase.\n   119→- As a coordinator, I can export the Google Form CSV and upload it in the app. It matches responses to existing talent by email and enriches their profiles in bulk.\n   120→- As a coordinator, when I open the Commentary panel for a competition, I see a smart \"Available Talent\" list — people who selected this competition in their survey, have Ready or Has Contact status, and aren't already booked on the same day.\n   121→- As a coordinator, I click \"Copy talent list\" and get a formatted list of names + phone numbers to paste into a group chat.\n   122→- As a coordinator, my homepage shows a pre-production alert panel with actionable items:\n   123→  - \"Start outreach for [Event] — no commentary assigned and it's 6 weeks away\"\n   124→  - \"⚠ No confirmed commentary for [Event] — it's 3 weeks away\"\n   125→  - \"Send calendar invite to [Name] for [Event] — they're confirmed but haven't received it\"\n   126→  - \"Schedule pre-production call for [Event] — it's 1 week away\"\n   127→  - \"Follow up with [Name] — invited 5 days ago, no booking response\"\n   128→- As a coordinator, completing an action (confirm talent, send invite, schedule meeting) clears the alert automatically.\n   129→\n   130→### Acceptance Criteria\n   131→- [ ] Public survey page at `/survey/:year` collects: WAG/MAG, event availability checkboxes, tech setup (upload/download Mbps, mic type, headphones), role preference, Discord status\n   132→- [ ] Submitting the survey writes to `talentRoster/{talentId}` (matched by email) or creates a pending entry\n   133→- [ ] CSV batch upload on settings page matches by email and updates profiles in bulk\n   134→- [ ] CommentaryPage shows \"Available Talent\" tab filtered by: survey availability + status (ready/has-contact) + no same-day conflict\n   135→- [ ] \"Copy talent list\" copies formatted `Name — Phone` lines to clipboard\n   136→- [ ] Homepage shows pre-production alert panel with all 5 alert types\n   137→- [ ] Completing each action causes its alert to disappear within 5 seconds (real-time Firebase sync)\n   138→\n   139→---\n   140→\n   141→## Bug Catalog\n   142→\n   143→No bugs cataloged yet. This PRD covers new feature development.\n   144→\n   145→---\n   146→\n   147→## Playwright Audit Results\n   148→\n   149→Not applicable — this is a new feature PRD. Discovery will verify plan integrity only.\n   150→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ed0abfc-b5cd-4068-9ec5-8c822e89ba45","uuid":"dc1fd3c3-fb8d-4687-93c4-fa1858a88b4f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM-2026-03-10.md","content":"# PRD: Commentary Talent CRM\n\n**Status:** NOT STARTED\n**Date:** 2026-03-10\n**Last Updated:** 2026-03-10\n\n---\n\n## Overview\nA full-stack CRM for coordinating 15–20+ gymnastics commentary talent across a season: migrating the\nexisting 428-contact Google Sheet into Firebase, adding self-service booking links, Gmail/GCal outreach,\nAI-powered talent discovery from alumni rosters, and automated pre-production alerts. Phase 1\n(Talent Roster UI) is already complete.\n\n## Test Competition / URL\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Competition ID | (use most recent competition in Firebase) |\n| Producer URL | `https://commentarygraphic.com/{compId}/producer` |\n| Commentary URL | `https://commentarygraphic.com/{compId}/commentary` |\n| Talent Roster | `https://commentarygraphic.com/talent` |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0 — Data Migration\n\n### User Stories\n- As a coordinator, I run a script once and all 428 people from my Google Sheet appear in the app — names, phones, emails, statuses, affiliations, and prior season counts.\n- As a coordinator, the 28 people who filled out the 2026 survey already have their tech info (internet speed, mic type, Discord status) populated.\n- As a coordinator, when I open a talent profile for someone like Tiara DeTommaso, I can see the meets she called last season in her history tab — that data came from the assignment sheet automatically.\n- As a coordinator, when the script encounters messy data (a phone field that says \"Barb said no\", or a duplicate with two slightly different spellings), it flags it in a log rather than crashing.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Running `node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js --dry-run` prints a summary (X created, Y enriched, Z assignments added, N flagged) without writing to Firebase\n- [ ] Running without `--dry-run` writes all 428 contacts to `talentRoster/` in Firebase\n- [ ] Survey responses (28 records) are merged into matching contacts by email\n- [ ] Competition assignments appear in each talent's `competitionHistory` array\n- [ ] Rows with malformed phone/email are flagged in a log file, not skipped silently\n- [ ] Duplicate names (fuzzy match > 90%) are flagged rather than creating two records\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Booking Links + Smart Availability\n\n### User Stories\n- As a coordinator, I click \"Generate Booking Link\" next to an assignment on the Commentary page. The app creates a unique URL I can copy and send via text or email.\n- As a talent invitee, I open the link on my phone (no login required) and see the event name, date, venue, and my assigned role. I click \"Yes, I'm available\" — that's it. The coordinator's app immediately shows me as Confirmed.\n- As a talent invitee, I click \"No, not this one\" and the app shows me the next 5 upcoming competitions. I can check the ones I could do. That interest is saved and the coordinator sees it automatically.\n- As a coordinator, I leave a note on a talent profile. The app parses that note and automatically flags her as interested in competitions mentioned in the note.\n- As a coordinator, when I'm looking at who to assign to a meet, I can see an \"Interested\" badge next to people who already flagged that competition as available.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] \"Generate Booking Link\" button appears next to each assignment in the Commentary page\n- [ ] Booking page at `/book/:token` loads without login and shows competition name, date, venue, and role\n- [ ] Clicking \"Yes\" updates assignment status to `confirmed` in Firebase immediately\n- [ ] Clicking \"No\" shows next 5 competitions with checkboxes; checking saves to `talentRoster/{id}/interested`\n- [ ] Adding a note with a date mention (e.g., \"available late February\") extracts and saves date hints to `interestedDates`\n- [ ] \"Interested\" badge appears in the talent search panel on CommentaryPage for people who flagged that competition\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — Gmail + Google Calendar\n\n### User Stories\n- As a coordinator, I complete a one-time Gmail OAuth setup. After that, I can send invite emails directly from the CommentaryPage — they come from my own Gmail address.\n- As a coordinator, every outreach button has a companion \"Copy for iMessage\" button that formats the message, copies it to clipboard, and logs it as sent when I confirm.\n- As a coordinator, I upload a screenshot of a text thread. The app reads it and extracts availability mentions, updating that talent's profile automatically.\n- As a coordinator, I click \"Send Briefing\" and the talent gets an email with: competition details, Virtius session URL, commentary talent view link, Discord room info, and pre-production meeting time.\n- As a coordinator, I click \"Send Calendar Invite\" and the talent gets a GCal event for competition day, 1 hour before start, with Discord info in the description.\n- As a coordinator, I pick a date for the pre-production call and click \"Schedule\" — a GCal invite goes to the talent's email and the meeting is logged in the app.\n- As a coordinator, every email I send appears in the talent's communication log on their profile page.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] \"Send Invite\" button on CommentaryPage sends email from coordinator's Gmail account\n- [ ] Every outreach button has a sibling \"Copy for iMessage\" button; confirming send logs the action\n- [ ] Screenshot upload on TalentProfilePage extracts availability text via Claude API and surfaces it as a note with extracted dates\n- [ ] \"Send Briefing\" sends a formatted email with all 5 required fields (competition, Virtius URL, commentary link, Discord, pre-prod time)\n- [ ] \"Send Calendar Invite\" creates a GCal event 1 hour before competition start with Discord info\n- [ ] \"Schedule Pre-Production\" creates a GCal event for the specified date/time\n- [ ] All sent communications appear in a \"Communications\" tab on TalentProfilePage with timestamp and type\n\n### Environment Variables Required (Phase 3 prerequisite)\nThe coordinator server (`server/.env` on `44.193.31.120`) needs:\n```\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...\nGOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=...\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4 — AI-Powered Discovery\n\n### User Stories\n- As a coordinator, I go to `/talent/discover`, select a school, and click \"Find Candidates.\" The app pulls the RTN alumni roster for that school.\n- As a coordinator, I see a list of candidate cards with suitability scores (1–5) and a brief explanation: \"Strong candidate — competed for 4 years, has a gymnastics podcast, active on Instagram.\"\n- As a coordinator, each card shows any social links Claude found (LinkedIn, Instagram) so I can quickly verify the person.\n- As a coordinator, I click \"Add to Roster\" on a promising candidate. They're added with status `need-info` (or `has-contact` if Claude found an email).\n- As a coordinator, if I run discovery on a school I've already run, the app recognizes existing records and shows \"already in roster\" on those cards.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `/talent/discover` page loads with a school name picker\n- [ ] Clicking \"Find Candidates\" fetches alumni data for the selected school and returns candidate cards\n- [ ] Each card shows: name, score (1–5), explanation, social links (if found)\n- [ ] \"Add to Roster\" creates a `talentRoster/` entry with status `need-info` or `has-contact`\n- [ ] Re-running discovery for the same school shows \"already in roster\" badge on existing records (no duplicates)\n\n### Environment Variables Required (Phase 4 prerequisite)\n```\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...  (on coordinator server)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5 — Annual Survey + Pre-Production Alerts\n\n### User Stories\n- As a coordinator, at the start of each season I send talent a link to `/survey/2027`. They fill it out and their answers go directly into Firebase.\n- As a coordinator, I can export the Google Form CSV and upload it in the app. It matches responses to existing talent by email and enriches their profiles in bulk.\n- As a coordinator, when I open the Commentary panel for a competition, I see a smart \"Available Talent\" list — people who selected this competition in their survey, have Ready or Has Contact status, and aren't already booked on the same day.\n- As a coordinator, I click \"Copy talent list\" and get a formatted list of names + phone numbers to paste into a group chat.\n- As a coordinator, my homepage shows a pre-production alert panel with actionable items:\n  - \"Start outreach for [Event] — no commentary assigned and it's 6 weeks away\"\n  - \"⚠ No confirmed commentary for [Event] — it's 3 weeks away\"\n  - \"Send calendar invite to [Name] for [Event] — they're confirmed but haven't received it\"\n  - \"Schedule pre-production call for [Event] — it's 1 week away\"\n  - \"Follow up with [Name] — invited 5 days ago, no booking response\"\n- As a coordinator, completing an action (confirm talent, send invite, schedule meeting) clears the alert automatically.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Public survey page at `/survey/:year` collects: WAG/MAG, event availability checkboxes, tech setup (upload/download Mbps, mic type, headphones), role preference, Discord status\n- [ ] Submitting the survey writes to `talentRoster/{talentId}` (matched by email) or creates a pending entry\n- [ ] CSV batch upload on settings page matches by email and updates profiles in bulk\n- [ ] CommentaryPage shows \"Available Talent\" tab filtered by: survey availability + status (ready/has-contact) + no same-day conflict\n- [ ] \"Copy talent list\" copies formatted `Name — Phone` lines to clipboard\n- [ ] Homepage shows pre-production alert panel with all 5 alert types\n- [ ] Completing each action causes its alert to disappear within 5 seconds (real-time Firebase sync)\n\n---\n\n## Bug Catalog\n\nNo bugs cataloged yet. This PRD covers new feature development.\n\n---\n\n## Playwright Audit Results\n\nNot applicable — this is a new feature PRD. Discovery will verify plan integrity only.\n","numLines":150,"startLine":1,"totalLines":150}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AkE8cFXNw8cYEMwqeVdCkb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Commentary Talent CRM — Implementation Plan\n     2→\n     3→**PRD:** PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM-2026-03-10.md\n     4→\n     5→> **Phase 1 (Talent Roster UI) is already complete.** This plan covers Phases 0, 2, 3, 4, 5.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Phases Overview\n    10→\n    11→| Phase | Description | Tasks | Status |\n    12→|-------|-------------|-------|--------|\n    13→| Phase 0 | Data Migration Script | 1 | COMPLETE |\n    14→| Phase 0-Deploy | Run migration + verify Firebase | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    15→| Phase 2 | Booking Links + Smart Availability | 6 | NOT STARTED |\n    16→| Phase 2-Deploy | Deploy Phase 2 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    17→| Phase 3 | Gmail + Google Calendar Outreach | 5 | NOT STARTED |\n    18→| Phase 3-Deploy | Deploy Phase 3 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    19→| Phase 4 | AI-Powered Talent Discovery | 5 | NOT STARTED |\n    20→| Phase 4-Deploy | Deploy Phase 4 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    21→| Phase 5 | Annual Survey + Pre-Production Alerts | 6 | NOT STARTED |\n    22→| Phase 5-Deploy | Deploy Phase 5 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    23→| Final-Deploy | Full acceptance criteria check | 2 | NOT STARTED |\n    24→| **Total** | | **30** | |\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→## Phase 0: Data Migration Script\n    29→\n    30→> **Deploy rule:** This is a server-side script, not a frontend build. The deploy task runs the script\n    31→> directly (no npm build needed). Firebase-only changes.\n    32→\n    33→### Task 0.1: Create CSV migration script — COMPLETE\n    34→\n    35→**File:** `server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js` (new file)\n    36→\n    37→**Change:** Create a Node.js script with the following behavior:\n    38→\n    39→```javascript\n    40→// Usage: node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js [--dry-run]\n    41→//\n    42→// Reads 3 CSVs:\n    43→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Master 2026_ Commentary Tracker - Commentators 2026.csv\n    44→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Master 2026_ Commentary Tracker - 2026 Assignment.csv\n    45→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Official Virtius Remote Commentary 2026 (Responses) - Form Responses 1 (6).csv\n    46→//\n    47→// Writes to Firebase: talentRoster/{talentId}\n    48→// Status mapping: \"Ready\" → \"ready\", \"Did 2025\" → \"did-2025\", \"Need Info\" → \"need-info\", \"Has Contact\" → \"has-contact\"\n    49→// Role mapping: \"Play by Play / Lead\" → \"pbp\", \"Color / Analyst\" → \"analyst\", \"Does not matter\" → \"both\"\n    50→// Dry-run: prints summary, no writes\n    51→// Flags: malformed phone/email, fuzzy duplicate names (>90% Levenshtein similarity)\n    52→// Outputs log: server/scripts/migration-log.json\n    53→// Summary line: \"X created, Y enriched (survey), Z assignments added, N flagged\"\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→**Firebase Admin initialization (required in script):**\n    57→```javascript\n    58→const path = require('path');\n    59→const admin = require('firebase-admin');\n    60→// Must run with GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS set (same as coordinator server)\n    61→admin.initializeApp({ credential: admin.credential.applicationDefault() });\n    62→const db = admin.database();\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→**CSV path resolution:** Use `path.resolve(__dirname, '../../', 'docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/...')` — paths are relative to the script file, not `process.cwd()`.\n    66→\n    67→**talentId format:** Generate as sanitized lowercase-dashed name: `name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')`. If a collision is detected (same key, different email), append `-2`, `-3` etc. This format is consistent with how other roster entries reference talent across phases.\n    68→\n    69→**Idempotency:** Before writing each record, check `talentRoster/{talentId}`. If it exists (match by email), UPDATE (merge) rather than overwrite. Log \"enriched\" for updates, \"created\" for new records.\n    70→\n    71→**compId mapping for history:** The assignment CSV has meet names/dates, not Firebase push-key IDs. There is no lookup table. Write `competitionHistory` using the raw meet name as a placeholder compId (e.g., `\"2025-01-18-stanford-vs-cal\"`). This data is informational; the `compId` field is best-effort and will not link to live Firebase competition records.\n    72→\n    73→Use `csv-parse` for CSV parsing (install if not present). Use a simple Levenshtein function for duplicate detection.\n    74→\n    75→**Schema written to Firebase:**\n    76→```json\n    77→{\n    78→  \"name\": \"First Last\",\n    79→  \"phone\": \"+1...\",\n    80→  \"email\": \"...\",\n    81→  \"wagMag\": \"WAG | MAG | Both\",\n    82→  \"commentaryRole\": \"pbp | analyst | both\",\n    83→  \"status\": \"ready | has-contact | did-2025 | need-info\",\n    84→  \"affiliation\": \"...\",\n    85→  \"conference\": \"...\",\n    86→  \"canProduce\": true,\n    87→  \"notes\": \"...\",\n    88→  \"competitionHistory\": [{ \"compId\": \"...\", \"role\": \"pbp\", \"date\": \"...\" }],\n    89→  \"surveyCompleted\": true,\n    90→  \"textSent\": true,\n    91→  \"discordAdded\": false,\n    92→  \"internetUploadMbps\": 50,\n    93→  \"internetDownloadMbps\": 100,\n    94→  \"createdAt\": \"ISO timestamp\",\n    95→  \"updatedAt\": \"ISO timestamp\"\n    96→}\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→**Implements:** Phase 0 acceptance criteria (dry-run, 428 contacts, survey enrichment, assignments, flagging)\n   100→\n   101→---\n   102→\n   103→## Phase 0-Deploy: Run Migration + Verify\n   104→\n   105→> **This is a deploy/run task.** No build needed — just run the script and verify Firebase.\n   106→\n   107→### Task 0-D.1: Run migration and verify data in Firebase — NOT STARTED\n   108→\n   109→**Steps:**\n   110→1. Create screenshots directory: `mkdir -p docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots`\n   111→2. Dry-run first: `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/opt/gymnastics-graphics/firebase-service-account.json node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js --dry-run`\n   112→3. Review output — confirm counts look correct (expect ~428 contacts)\n   113→4. Live run: `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/opt/gymnastics-graphics/firebase-service-account.json node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js`\n   114→5. Navigate to `https://commentarygraphic.com/talent` with Playwright\n   115→6. Take screenshot → `docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots/verify-phase0-talent-list.png`\n   116→7. Verify talent count shown matches expected (~428)\n   117→\n   118→**Checks:**\n   119→- [ ] No crash during dry-run\n   120→- [ ] Live run creates records in Firebase `talentRoster/`\n   121→- [ ] Talent page shows records (not empty)\n   122→- [ ] migration-log.json exists and lists flagged rows\n   123→\n   124→---\n   125→\n   126→## Phase 2: Booking Links + Smart Availability\n   127→\n   128→> **Deploy rule:** Commit each task. Do NOT deploy until Phase 2-Deploy.\n   129→> **Prerequisite:** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` must be set in server `.env` on `44.193.31.120` (used by Task 2.4 note parsing endpoint).\n   130→\n   131→### Task 2.1: Add booking token server endpoints — NOT STARTED\n   132→\n   133→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   134→\n   135→**Architecture note:** `BookingPage` is a public page accessed by talent (no login, no session). The coordinator server (`44.193.31.120:3003`) has an auto-shutdown feature and may be offline when a talent clicks a link 2 weeks later. The frontend has no established pattern for calling the coordinator directly from the browser.\n   136→\n   137→**Solution: BookingPage reads/writes Firebase directly, not via coordinator.** Only the token generation endpoint (called by the authenticated coordinator UI) goes through the coordinator server. All public-facing operations use Firebase with appropriate security rules.\n   138→\n   139→```javascript\n   140→// POST /api/book/generate — creates a booking token (coordinator-side, auth required)\n   141→// Body: { talentId, compId, role }\n   142→// Writes: bookingTokens/{uuid} = { talentId, compId, role, createdAt, expiresAt (30 days from now, ISO), responded: false }\n   143→// Also updates: competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}.status = 'invited', invitedAt = now\n   144→// Returns: { token, url: `https://commentarygraphic.com/book/${uuid}` }\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→**Public-facing (BookingPage reads Firebase directly, no coordinator):**\n   148→```javascript\n   149→// BookingPage reads these Firebase paths directly:\n   150→//   bookingTokens/{token}          → token metadata (talentId, compId, role, expiresAt, responded)\n   151→//   competitions/{compId}/config   → { eventName, meetDate, venue }\n   152→//   talentRoster/{talentId}        → { name }\n   153→//\n   154→// BookingPage writes these Firebase paths directly:\n   155→//   On \"Yes\":\n   156→//     competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}: { status: 'confirmed', confirmedAt: now }\n   157→//     bookingTokens/{token}: { responded: true, response: 'yes' }\n   158→//\n   159→//   On \"No\" (save interested comps):\n   160→//     For each selected compId: talentRoster/{talentId}/interested/{compId} = true\n   161→//     (keyed object, not array — avoids overwriting previous interests)\n   162→//     bookingTokens/{token}: { responded: true, response: 'no' }\n   163→//\n   164→// BookingPage fetches upcoming competitions from Firebase:\n   165→//   competitions/ — filter by config.meetDate > now, exclude original compId\n   166→//   Show next 5 sorted by meetDate asc\n   167→//\n   168→// Expiry + double-response guards (client-side):\n   169→//   If token.expiresAt < now → show \"This link has expired\"\n   170→//   If token.responded === true → show \"You've already responded\"\n   171→```\n   172→\n   173→**Firebase security rules update required** (in `database.rules.json`):\n   174→```json\n   175→\"bookingTokens\": {\n   176→  \"$token\": {\n   177→    \".read\": true,\n   178→    \".write\": \"auth == null || auth != null\"\n   179→  }\n   180→}\n   181→```\n   182→(public read of token; public write to `responded` and `response` fields — scope carefully)\n   183→\n   184→**Implements:** Booking token generation, Yes/No response flow\n   185→\n   186→---\n   187→\n   188→### Task 2.2: Create public BookingPage — NOT STARTED\n   189→\n   190→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/BookingPage.jsx` (new file)\n   191→\n   192→**Change:** Create a public page (no auth required) that reads/writes Firebase directly (NOT the coordinator server — see Task 2.1 architecture note):\n   193→- Imports `{ db, ref, get, update, set }` from `../lib/firebase`\n   194→- Reads `bookingTokens/{token}`, `competitions/{compId}/config`, `talentRoster/{talentId}` on load\n   195→- Guards: if token expired → \"This link has expired\"; if already responded → \"You've already responded\"\n   196→- Shows: competition eventName, meetDate, venue, talent's name, assigned role\n   197→- Has two primary buttons: \"Yes, I'm available\" and \"No, not this one\"\n   198→- On \"Yes\": writes to Firebase directly (see Task 2.1), shows confirmation screen\n   199→- On \"No\": queries `competitions/` from Firebase, filters meetDate > now, shows next 5 as checkboxes; submit writes `talentRoster/{talentId}/interested/{compId} = true` for each checked\n   200→- Mobile-first layout (talent opens this on their phone)\n   201→- No navbar, no auth, standalone page with minimal styling\n   202→\n   203→Reference `../lib/firebase` import pattern from `useCommentaryStaff.js`.\n   204→\n   205→**Implements:** Public booking response flow\n   206→\n   207→---\n   208→\n   209→### Task 2.3: Add public route for booking page — NOT STARTED\n   210→\n   211→**File:** `show-controller/src/App.jsx`\n   212→\n   213→**Change:** Add `/book/:token` route that renders BookingPage without auth guard:\n   214→\n   215→```jsx\n   216→// CRITICAL: Place BEFORE the <Route path=\"/:compId\"> wildcard (App.jsx line ~101)\n   217→// or the router will treat \"book\" as a competition ID.\n   218→// App.jsx has no global auth wrapper — just insert before the /:compId route.\n   219→<Route path=\"/book/:token\" element={<BookingPage />} />\n   220→```\n   221→\n   222→There is no global auth wrapper in App.jsx (only `<CoordinatorGate>` wraps `/_admin/vm-pool`).\n   223→The route must be placed before `<Route path=\"/:compId\" element={<CompetitionLayout />}>`.\n   224→Read App.jsx first to confirm placement.\n   225→\n   226→**Implements:** Public access to booking page\n   227→\n   228→---\n   229→\n   230→### Task 2.4: Add note parsing endpoint — NOT STARTED\n   231→\n   232→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   233→\n   234→**Change:** Add a new endpoint that calls Claude API to extract date hints from talent notes:\n   235→\n   236→```javascript\n   237→// POST /api/talent/:talentId/notes/parse\n   238→// Body: { noteText: \"She's available late February but busy Jan 15\" }\n   239→// Calls Claude API (claude-haiku-4-5-20251001) with prompt:\n   240→//   \"Extract any date mentions or availability hints from this note.\n   241→//    Return JSON: { availablePeriods: ['late February'], unavailableDates: ['January 15'] }\"\n   242→// Writes parsed hints to talentRoster/{talentId}.parsedAvailability = { ... }\n   243→// Returns: { availablePeriods, unavailableDates }\n   244→```\n   245→\n   246→Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in server `.env`. Use the `@anthropic-ai/sdk` package.\n   247→\n   248→**Implements:** AI note parsing for availability tracking\n   249→\n   250→---\n   251→\n   252→### Task 2.5: Add \"Interested\" badge + note parsing trigger to TalentProfilePage — NOT STARTED\n   253→\n   254→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/TalentProfilePage.jsx`\n   255→\n   256→**Change:**\n   257→1. When a note is saved (existing \"Save Notes\" button), also call `POST /api/talent/:talentId/notes/parse` with the note text\n   258→2. Show any parsed availability periods as small tags below the notes field: `Available: late February` (green), `Busy: January 15` (red)\n   259→3. These tags are read from `talent.parsedAvailability.availablePeriods` and `unavailableDates`\n   260→\n   261→**Implements:** Visual feedback for AI-parsed availability\n   262→\n   263→---\n   264→\n   265→### Task 2.6: Add booking link generation + Interested badge to CommentaryPage — NOT STARTED\n   266→\n   267→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/CommentaryPage.jsx`\n   268→\n   269→**Change:**\n   270→1. Next to each assigned talent in the assignments list, add a small \"🔗 Copy Link\" button\n   271→2. Clicking \"🔗 Copy Link\" calls `POST /api/book/generate` with `{ talentId, compId, role }`, then copies the returned URL to clipboard\n   272→3. Show a small \"Copied!\" toast for 2 seconds\n   273→4. In the talent search panel (right side), show an \"Interested\" badge (green pill: \"Interested ✓\") next to any talent whose `talentRoster/{id}.interested` array contains the current `compId`\n   274→\n   275→**Implements:** Booking link generation, interested badge in assignment panel\n   276→\n   277→---\n   278→\n   279→## Phase 2-Deploy: Deploy Phase 2 Changes\n   280→\n   281→> **This is a deploy task.** Build frontend + deploy coordinator server changes.\n   282→\n   283→### Task 2-D.1: Build, deploy, and verify Phase 2 — NOT STARTED\n   284→\n   285→**Frontend changed?** Yes (`BookingPage.jsx`, `App.jsx`, `CommentaryPage.jsx`, `TalentProfilePage.jsx`)\n   286→```bash\n   287→cd show-controller && npm run build\n   288→# then upload dist per CLAUDE.md Step 1\n   289→```\n   290→\n   291→**Server changed?** Yes (`server/index.js` — new endpoints)\n   292→```bash\n   293→# SSH to coordinator (44.193.31.120)\n   294→# cd /opt/gymnastics-graphics\n   295→# git pull origin main\n   296→# pm2 restart coordinator (with GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS per CLAUDE.md)\n   297→```\n   298→\n   299→**Verify:**\n   300→- [ ] Navigate to `/talent` — no console errors\n   301→- [ ] Open a competition's commentary page — \"🔗 Copy Link\" button appears next to assignments\n   302→- [ ] Navigate to `/book/test-token-invalid` — BookingPage loads (may show error for invalid token, but page renders)\n   303→- [ ] Take screenshot → `docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots/verify-phase2-booking-link.png`\n   304→\n   305→---\n   306→\n   307→## Phase 3: Gmail + Google Calendar Outreach\n   308→\n   309→> **Deploy rule:** Commit each task. Do NOT deploy until Phase 3-Deploy.\n   310→> **Prerequisite:** `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN` must be set in server `.env` on `44.193.31.120`.\n   311→\n   312→### Task 3.1: Create Gmail service — NOT STARTED\n   313→\n   314→**File:** `server/lib/gmailService.js` (new file)\n   315→\n   316→**Change:** Create a Gmail OAuth service using `googleapis` npm package:\n   317→\n   318→```javascript\n   319→// gmailService.js exports:\n   320→// sendEmail({ to, subject, html }) — sends via coordinator's Gmail account\n   321→// Uses OAuth2 with GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN from process.env\n   322→// Returns message ID on success, throws on failure\n   323→\n   324→// Email templates (inline):\n   325→// - inviteEmail(talent, competition, role, bookingUrl) → HTML invite with event details + booking link\n   326→//   NOTE: bookingUrl is required — the invite endpoint (Task 3.3) must generate the token FIRST\n   327→// - briefingEmail(talent, competition, virtiusUrl, discordInfo, preProdTime) → HTML briefing\n   328→// - reminderEmail(talent, competition, bookingUrl) → HTML reminder with booking link\n   329→```\n   330→\n   331→Install `googleapis` if not already in `server/package.json`.\n   332→\n   333→**Implements:** Gmail outreach capability\n   334→\n   335→---\n   336→\n   337→### Task 3.2: Create Google Calendar service — NOT STARTED\n   338→\n   339→**File:** `server/lib/googleCalendarService.js` (new file)\n   340→\n   341→**Change:** Create a GCal service using `googleapis`:\n   342→\n   343→```javascript\n   344→// googleCalendarService.js exports:\n   345→// createCompetitionEvent({ talentEmail, competitionName, startTime, discordInfo })\n   346→//   → Creates GCal event 1 hour before startTime, adds talent as attendee\n   347→//   → Returns eventId\n   348→//\n   349→// createPreProdMeeting({ talentEmail, meetingTime, competitionName })\n   350→//   → Creates GCal event at meetingTime\n   351→//   → Returns eventId\n   352→```\n   353→\n   354→**Implements:** Calendar invite capability\n   355→\n   356→---\n   357→\n   358→### Task 3.3: Add outreach API endpoints — NOT STARTED\n   359→\n   360→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   361→\n   362→**Change:** Add outreach endpoints (import gmailService and googleCalendarService at top):\n   363→\n   364→```javascript\n   365→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/invite\n   366→//   Step 1: Generate a booking token (reuse Task 2.1 token generation logic)\n   367→//           bookingTokens/{uuid} = { talentId, compId, role, ... }\n   368→//           bookingUrl = `https://commentarygraphic.com/book/${uuid}`\n   369→//   Step 2: Send invite email via gmailService.sendEmail(inviteEmail(talent, competition, role, bookingUrl))\n   370→//   Step 3: Update competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}: { status: 'invited', invitedAt: now }\n   371→//   Step 4: Append to communicationLog (see log shape below)\n   372→\n   373→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/briefing\n   374→//   Body: { virtiusUrl: string, discordInfo: string, preProdTime: ISO string }\n   375→//   All three fields are required — return 400 if any are missing\n   376→//   Sends briefing email, updates .briefedAt = now, status = 'briefed'\n   377→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   378→\n   379→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/calendar-invite\n   380→//   Creates GCal event 1 hour before competition start (read meetDate from competitions/{compId}/config)\n   381→//   Updates .calendarInviteSent = true\n   382→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   383→\n   384→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/schedule-preproduction\n   385→//   Body: { meetingTime: ISO string }\n   386→//   Creates pre-prod GCal event, adds talent as attendee\n   387→//   Updates .preProductionMeetingScheduled = meetingTime\n   388→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   389→\n   390→// communicationLog — use Firebase push keys, NOT an array:\n   391→//   talentRoster/{talentId}/communicationLog/{pushKey} = { type, sentAt, note }\n   392→//   Firebase RTDB has no arrayUnion — push keys avoid read-then-write race conditions\n   393→// Log entry shape: { type: 'invite'|'briefing'|'calendar'|'preproduction'|'imessage', sentAt: ISO, note: '...' }\n   394→```\n   395→\n   396→**Implements:** All outreach server actions\n   397→\n   398→---\n   399→\n   400→### Task 3.4: Add outreach buttons to CommentaryPage — NOT STARTED\n   401→\n   402→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/CommentaryPage.jsx`\n   403→\n   404→**Change:** In the assignment detail view (when a talent card is expanded/selected):\n   405→1. Add outreach action buttons: \"Send Invite\", \"Send Briefing\", \"Calendar Invite\", \"Schedule Pre-Prod\"\n   406→2. \"Send Invite\" calls endpoint directly (endpoint generates token internally — no extra input needed)\n   407→3. \"Send Briefing\" must open a small modal first to collect 3 required fields:\n   408→   - Virtius session URL (text input)\n   409→   - Discord info (text input, e.g. room name/link)\n   410→   - Pre-production meeting time (datetime-local input)\n   411→   Only after the coordinator fills these and clicks \"Send\" does the modal call the briefing endpoint.\n   412→   Without this modal, the briefing endpoint has no data to put in the email.\n   413→4. \"Schedule Pre-Prod\" opens a datetime picker modal; submits `{ meetingTime }` to endpoint\n   414→5. Each button has a sibling \"📋 Copy for iMessage\" button that:\n   415→   - Formats the same message as the email (plain text)\n   416→   - Copies to clipboard\n   417→   - Shows: \"Sent via iMessage?\" → [Yes] → logs `{ type: 'imessage', sentAt: now }` to server\n   418→6. Show a \"Sent ✓\" indicator when the server confirms the email was sent\n   419→\n   420→**Implements:** Coordinator-facing outreach UI\n   421→\n   422→---\n   423→\n   424→### Task 3.5: Add screenshot upload + communications tab to TalentProfilePage — NOT STARTED\n   425→\n   426→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/TalentProfilePage.jsx`\n   427→\n   428→**Change:**\n   429→1. Add a \"Communications\" tab alongside the existing profile sections\n   430→2. Communications tab shows `talent.communicationLog` entries sorted by `sentAt` desc, showing type + timestamp + note\n   431→3. Add a \"Upload Screenshot\" button — accepts image file, converts to base64, sends to a new endpoint `POST /api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot` which calls Claude API vision to extract availability text from the screenshot\n   432→4. Extracted text appears as a new note with prefix `[From screenshot] ` and triggers note parsing\n   433→\n   434→Add new server endpoint:\n   435→```javascript\n   436→// POST /api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot\n   437→// Body: { imageBase64, mimeType }\n   438→// Calls Claude API with image, extracts availability mentions\n   439→// Returns: { extractedText, availablePeriods, unavailableDates }\n   440→// Writes extracted note to talent's notes field (prepended)\n   441→//\n   442→// IMPORTANT: Add body size limit for this endpoint — screenshots base64-encoded are 2–7MB.\n   443→// Express default JSON limit is 100KB. Add before this route:\n   444→//   app.use('/api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot', express.json({ limit: '10mb' }));\n   445→```\n   446→\n   447→**Implements:** Communication log UI, screenshot-to-availability parsing\n   448→\n   449→---\n   450→\n   451→## Phase 3-Deploy: Deploy Phase 3 Changes\n   452→\n   